  "notes": "Government counter-clerk intake tool. Strong semantic color system: red (#9f2328 on #fdf4f4) = disqualifying, amber (#7d5200 on #fdf1d2/#fffdf6 with #e3b953 border) = curable by deadline, green (#1d6b3e) = met/complete; whole cards are tinted and bordered by severity, and mismatched record values are rendered in bold red inline. Header shows a persistent deadline with a gold live countdown ('3 d 1 h 7 m remaining'). Status pills are fully rounded (999px) while panels use 6-10px radius and buttons 4px. Each failing check carries 'To resolve:' text, a cure-deadline line, and an inline remediation form (record payment, amend ballot name, refer to supervisor). The 'Deficiency notice' tab renders a print-styled formal letter with bordered tables. Disposition card has a thick red left rule. No icons or imagery; ✓ glyphs inside chips only."
}
